<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  313 Help collects nothing and tracks nobody (docs/08). This file says so in Apple's own terms.

	  NSPrivacyTracking: false. There is no advertising identifier, no third-party SDK of any kind, and nothing
	  the app sends could be joined to a person or a device: a report carries a listing id, a kind, an optional
	  note, a minute-precision time, and sha256(random on-device key ‖ target ‖ day), which differs for every
	  target and every day.

	  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes: empty. Reports and proposals are text a person chooses to send about a place,
	  not data collected about the person. If the store questionnaire asks, that is "User Content", not linked to
	  identity and not used for tracking. Location is used on the device to sort a list by distance and is never
	  written down or sent, so it is not collected either.

	  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes: empty. The app uses no required-reason API. It keeps its own state in files it
	  creates (not UserDefaults), never reads file timestamps, never asks for free disk space, never reads system
	  boot time, and never looks at the active keyboard list. If any of that changes, add the category and reason
	  here in the same commit.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
